The  driver  supports the Promise Ultra33, Ultra66, Ultra100, Ul‐
tra100TX2, Ultra100TX2v2, Ultra133,  Ultra133TX2,  Ultra133TX2v2,
Fasttrak133  and Serial ATA/150 IDE controllers, and provides the
interface with the hardware for  the  driver.   The  0x0002  flag
forces  the driver to disable DMA on chipsets for which DMA would
normally be enabled.  This can be used as a debugging aid, or  to
work  around problems where the IDE controller is wired up to the
system incorrectly.  The timings used for the PIO and  DMA  modes
for  controllers  listed above are for a PCI bus running at 30 or
33 MHz.  This driver may not work properly  on  overclocked  sys‐
